    "intro_html":  "This is the bowl every Vietnamese lunch spot builds its reputation on. Chicken thighs marinated in lemongrass, fish sauce, garlic, and honey, roasted until the edges caramelize, then piled over rice with cucumber, carrot, and cilantro and drenched in nuoc cham. It has a strong protein-per-calorie ratio: 668 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e58 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.89 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
